It is a little past one o'clock.
I walk slowly over to the medical clinic.
It is a short trip, but I am still very sore and tired.
I take out my yellow health card.
The sun is shining outside.
But I ought to wear sunglasses, because the light hurts my eyes.
I enter the clinic's reception.
A small machine hangs on the wall.
You always have to scan your yellow health card here.
I got the card in the mail when I moved to Denmark.
I scan the yellow card on the machine.
It makes a little sound and flashes green.
That means that the doctor knows I am here.
I walk into the actual waiting room.
I sit down on an empty chair and wait.
